server/node_modules
client/node_modules
node_modules
.DS_Store   
.env

# Build output. Compiled JS must never be tracked: it drifts from source, and a
# git-based deploy that pulls a stale dist/ serves code nobody wrote. The image
# builds it from source on target; `npm run build` makes it locally.
server/dist
client/dist
dist

# The legacy SQLite database. Postgres has held the authoritative data since
# the 2026-10-25 import (140 weather days, 6 fills, 7 readings, 15 hvac reports).
# The file stays on disk as the untouched source it was imported from, and in
# git history at ed40e68 and earlier, but it is no longer tracked: a tracked
# database drifts from the real one and invites a future script to read the
# stale copy and report it as current.
data/*.db
data/*.db-shm
data/*.db-wal
#
# CORRECTION, 2026-10-26. The note above said the file "stays on disk as the
# untouched source". Both halves were wrong.
#
# It did NOT survive branch switching: once the files left the index, moving
# between commits removed the working copies and the data/ directory with them.
# Recovered from history -- git show 1bd64df:data/fuel_tracker.db-wal and the
# .db beside it.
#
# And a .db alone was never the source. 30 of the 109 weather days and 2 of the
# 15 hvac reports live ONLY in fuel_tracker.db-wal; the main file alone reads
# 79 days. ANY copy of this database is the PAIR or it is incomplete -- and
# incomplete silently, because an import of 79 rows verifies perfectly against
# the 79 it attempted.
#
# Postgres is authoritative now. If the legacy data is ever needed again, take
# the .db and the -wal together.
